NEXT, on the machine that has BOTH directories:
  for a in kmeans knn dbscan; do
    diff <(grep '^input\.' A/$a.hashes) <(grep '^input\.' B/$a.hashes) \
      || echo "$a: INPUTS DIFFER -- stop, the fixtures are not the same bytes"
    python3 tools/identity_trace_diff.py A/$a.card B/$a.card
  done

Read the k-NN card knowing knn.out_dist/out_idx are PRE-SORT (an arm's
internal order, which the two arms genuinely disagree about) and
knn.sorted_dist/sorted_idx are what the caller gets. Sorted distances
agreeing over sorted indices differing = the selector chose different
members of an equidistant class, and nothing else diverged.
